{"Empty Calendar Array Crashes: Several changed callers now pass destinationCalendar: [] when no booking or user calendar exists. For a Google Meet booking in that state, mainHostDestinationCalendar is undefined, so this line throws before the fallback to Cal Video can run and the booking flow fails.": 0.24335239827632904, "Missing External Id Loses Fallback: When an older booking reference has no externalCalendarId, this fallback searches for a destination whose externalId is also undefined, so it never uses the selected destination calendar. Google update requests can then be sent with no calendar id, making edits or reschedules fail even when event.destinationCalendar[0] is available.": 0.8682756423950195, "Organization Slug Flag Reversed: This flips the previous organization slug behavior. When team billing is disabled, new organizations are now created without slug; when it is enabled, the slug is persisted immediately and also stored as requestedSlug, which can make new orgs inaccessible or bypass the requested-slug flow.": 0.8691679835319519, "Current Destination Is Dropped: This loop resolves the credential for each destination, but the current destination calendar id is not passed through to most providers. In a collective booking with mixed calendars, such as Google first and Office365 second, the Office365 provider still reads event.destinationCalendar[0] and can post to the wrong calendar id or fail, so later hosts do not get their calendar event.": 0.9433565735816956, "Recurring Deletes Repeat Per Reference: The new outer loop iterates every calendar reference, but this recurring cleanup branch still loops all user calendar credentials and then picks the first _calendar reference from each updated booking. With multiple calendar references, the same cleanup can run once per reference and pair a credential with the wrong booking reference, causing duplicate or mis-targeted external deletes.": 0.9068110585212708}